"align\":\"start\",\"text\":\"&lt;p&gt;To minimize the average waiting time, the jobs should be scheduled using the &lt;strong&gt;Shortest Processing Time (SPT)&lt;/strong&gt; rule (also known as Shortest Job First).&lt;/p&gt;\\n&lt;h3&gt;Reasoning:&lt;/h3&gt;\\n&lt;p&gt;If the jobs are executed in the order of their processing times $t_1, t_2, t_3, t_4, t_5$:&lt;/p&gt;\\n&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The 1st job waits $0$ minutes.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The 2nd job waits $t_1$ minutes.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The 3rd job waits $t_1 + t_2$ minutes.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The 4th job waits $t_1 + t_2 + t_3$ minutes.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The 5th job waits $t_1 + t_2 + t_3 + t_4$ minutes.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\\n&lt;p&gt;The total waiting time is:&lt;br /&gt;\\n$$\\\\text{Total Wait Time} = 4t_1 + 3t_2 + 2t_3 + 1t_4$$&lt;/p&gt;\\n&lt;p&gt;Because the earlier processing times are added into the wait times of all subsequent jobs, they carry the largest multipliers (weights). To minimize this sum, the smallest values must be paired with the largest multipliers. Therefore, the jobs must be processed in ascending order of their duration.&lt;/p&gt;\\n&lt;p&gt;Sorting the given print times ${2, 4, 1, 8, 3}$ from shortest to longest gives:&lt;br /&gt;\\n$1, 2, 3, 4, 8$&lt;/p&gt;\\n&lt;p&gt;Order: 1, 2, 3, 4, 8&lt;/p&gt;\\n\"}}]}}]}},{\"type\":\"object\",\"name\":\"panel.models.layout.Column\",\"id\":\"2084e958-86e0-4beb-a074-aefa64c82f6e\",\"attributes\":{\"name\":\"Column00190\",\"css_classes\":[\"footer\"],\"stylesheets\":[\"\\n:host(.pn-loading):before, .pn-loading:before {\\n  background-color: #c3c3c3;\\n  width: calc(min(40px, 300px));\\n  height: calc(min(40px, 300px));\\n  mask-size: calc(min(40px, 300px)) calc(min(40px, 300px));\\n  -webkit-mask-size: calc(min(40px, 300px)) calc(min(40px, 300px));\\n}\",{\"id\":\"24f5d056-496d-46fd-9cb7-af5022eece36\"},{\"id\":\"2604a700-b98c-40a5-9ae0-67f093748cfa\"},{\"id\":\"6b850f0f-721d-41f2-8ab1-5f30d70222c0\"},{\"id\":\"7406f8ae-2